I built the issue desk in `src/` (`main.ts` exports `Model`, `init`, `update`, `view`; logic is split across `message.ts`, `command.ts`, `model.ts`, `update.ts`, `view.ts`, `domain.ts`). `./check` passes and all 30 visible tests pass; I also drove the main flows in headless Chromium with no page errors. Uncertain points: whitespace-only names count as empty, post and label adds are disabled until comments or labels have loaded, error lines use prefixes like `assign error:` and `label error:` that the brief did not spell out, and the buttons' visible text ("Retry", "Add label", "Light", "Dark") is my wording. The browser test runs used 7 of the 15 `./check`/`./test` allowance.